rix may have zeros, idf may be zero? But idf should be positive. We'll just compute.\n\nWe need to import math for sqrt.\n\nImplement solve(case) that returns dict.\n\nNow we need to produce Python source as JSON string. The entire response must be a JSON object with key \"implementation\" whose value is the Python source string.\n\nWe must follow strict submission envelope. So output:\n\n{\n  \"implementation\": \"import math\\n\\ndef solve(case):\\n    matrix = case['matrix']\\n    idf = case['idf']\\n    vector = case['vector']\\n    n = len(matrix)\\n    m = len(idf)\\n    if n == 0 or m == 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Empty matrix or idf\\\")\\n    # Validate matrix dimensions\\n    for row in matrix:\\n        if len(row) != m:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"Inconsistent matrix row length\\\")\\n    if len(vector) != n:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Vector length mismatch\\\")\\n    # Compute X (feature matrix scaled by idf)\\n    X = [[matrix[i][j] * idf[j] for j in range(m)] for i in range(n)]\\n    # Compute degree (squared norm per row) with floor\\n    floor = 1e-10\\n    degree = []\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        sum_sq = sum(X[i][j] * X[i][j] for j in range(m))\\n        degree.append(max(sum_sq, floor))\\n    # Precompute inverse sqrt of degree\\n    inv_sqrt_deg = [1.0 / math.sqrt(d) for d in degree]\\n    # Scale input vector\\n    scaled_vec = [vector[i] * inv_sqrt_deg[i] for i in range(n)]\\n    # Compute v = X^T * scaled_vec\\n    v = [0.0] * m\\n    for j in range(m):\\n        s = 0.0\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            s += X[i][j] * scaled_vec[i]\\n        v[j] = s\\n    # Compute w = X * v\\n    w = [0.0] * n\\n    for i in range(n):\\n        s = 0.0\\n        for j in range(m):\\n            s += X[i][j] * v[j]\\n        w[i] = s\\n    # Rescale rows: result = inv_sqrt_deg * w\\n    result = [w[i] * inv_sqrt_deg[i] for i in range(n)]\\n    return {\\\"degree\\\": degree, \\\"result\\\": result}\"\n}\n\nBut need to ensur